# Everything the image build does not need.
#
# The Dockerfile restores and builds from source inside the image, so build output on the
# host is not only useless to it, it is most of the upload.
#
# Every project path is spelled out in full, with no wildcard inside it. The az CLI packer
# does not reliably honour `**/bin/`, and it does not honour a `*` standing in for a single
# path segment either: `src/*/bin/` looks right and still lets gigabytes of build output
# through. The failure is worse than a slow upload, because it does not fail. The client sits
# there packing with nothing on screen and no run ever appears in the registry.
#
# If a project is added, add its two lines here. That is the whole maintenance burden, and it
# is cheaper than working out why a build never starts.

src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Api/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Api/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Connectors/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Connectors/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Data/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Data/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Dataverse/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Dataverse/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Domain/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Domain/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Export/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Export/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Jobs/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Jobs/obj
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Pipeline/bin
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Pipeline/obj
tests/PowerPete.Analyzer.Tests/bin
tests/PowerPete.Analyzer.Tests/obj
tests/PowerPete.Analyzer.Tests/TestResults

# The web build runs inside the image and installs its own packages.
src/web/node_modules
src/web/dist

# Produced inside the image, not copied into it. The build stage creates the directory
# itself, so there is no placeholder to keep an exception for.
src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Api/wwwroot

# Kept as a second line of defence, for anything outside a known project.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
bin/
obj/
node_modules/

# NOT excluded, deliberately: src/PowerPete.Analyzer.Domain/Generated and
# db/migrations/*.generated.sql. Both are gitignored because they are rebuilt from the
# contracts, and both have to reach the image because the SDK stage has no PowerShell to
# rebuild them with. The Dockerfile checks they arrived.

.git
.github
.azure
.vscode
.claude
.playwright-mcp
artifacts
*.user
*.suo
*.png
